    <!-- ══ BENEFIT ROWS: UV + ENERGY ══ -->
    <section class="of-benefits">
      <div class="of-benefits__container">

        <div class="of-benefits__header">
          <div class="of-benefits__eyebrow">The Benefits</div>
          <h2 class="of-benefits__headline">What Office Window Film Actually Does</h2>
          <p class="of-benefits__intro">Solar heat, UV, glare, privacy — tackled in a single professional installation. No window replacement, no renovation, no downtime.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 1: UV Protection — image LEFT, text RIGHT -->
        <div class="of-row">
          <div class="of-row__image">
            <img
              src="/images/office-uv-protection-window-film.jpg"
              alt="Philadelphia office window with UV-protective window film — healthy plants and preserved furnishings near filtered sunlight"
              width="680" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="of-row__text">
            <div class="of-row__eyebrow">Benefit 01 · UV Protection</div>
            <h3 class="of-row__title">Block 99% of UV rays — protect people and everything inside</h3>
            <p class="of-row__body">Standard window glass blocks almost no UV radiation. Employees who work near windows receive cumulative UV-A and UV-B exposure equivalent to outdoor workers — without the awareness that typically comes with stepping outside. Over years, this contributes to elevated skin cancer risk for window-adjacent staff.</p>
            <blockquote class="of-pullquote">
              <p class="of-pullquote__text">“While window glass blocks most UVB rays, UVA rays — which can lead to premature aging and skin damage — still get through.”</p>
              <cite class="of-pullquote__cite"><a href="https://www.skincancer.org/blog/window-film/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Skin Cancer Foundation — skincancer.org</a></cite>
            </blockquote>
            <p class="of-row__body">Beyond health, UV is the primary driver of interior fading. Carpets, branded upholstery, artwork, and wood furniture all degrade irreversibly under chronic UV exposure. Professional-grade window films block up to 99.9% of UV transmission from day one — with no visible change to how the space looks.</p>
            <ul class="of-row__bullets">
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                99.9% UV rejection — confirmed by 3M Prestige 70 technical data sheet
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                Slows fading of carpet, artwork, branded interiors, and wood furniture
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                The Skin Cancer Foundation recommends UV-blocking window films for indoor skin protection
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 2: Energy Savings — text LEFT, image RIGHT -->
        <div class="of-row of-row--rev">
          <div class="of-row__image">
            <img
              src="/images/office-energy-savings-window-film.jpg"
              alt="Philadelphia commercial office building with energy-efficient window film — reduced HVAC load and lower cooling costs"
              width="680" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="of-row__text">
            <div class="of-row__eyebrow">Benefit 02 · Energy Savings</div>
            <h3 class="of-row__title">Cut cooling costs up to 30% — without replacing a window</h3>
            <p class="of-row__body">Solar heat gain through untreated glass accounts for approximately 33% of commercial cooling costs (3M). A west-facing wall of windows adds the equivalent heat output of multiple space heaters — continuously, all afternoon, every summer day. Your HVAC fights this load around the clock.</p>
            <p class="of-row__body">Solar control window film addresses the root cause: it rejects heat at the glass before it becomes an HVAC problem. The 3M Prestige 70 — the most common choice for Philadelphia offices — delivers a Solar Heat Gain Coefficient of 0.50 vs. 0.81 for untreated single-pane clear glass, a 38% heat gain reduction. See our full guide to <a href="/benefits/energy-savings/">energy-saving window film for Philadelphia buildings</a> — payback is typically 3–5 years.</p>
            <ul class="of-row__bullets">
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                Up to 30% reduction in summer cooling costs for commercial buildings
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                3M Prestige 70: SHGC 0.50 vs. 0.81 untreated — 38% heat gain reduction
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                3–5 year payback period — then 10+ years of continued savings
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 3: Glare Control — image LEFT, text RIGHT -->
        <div class="of-row">
          <div class="of-row__image">
            <img
              src="/images/office-glare-control-window-film.jpg"
              alt="Philadelphia office worker comfortable at workstation with glare-free screens — soft filtered light through window film"
              width="680" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="of-row__text">
            <div class="of-row__eyebrow">Benefit 03 · Glare Control</div>
            <h3 class="of-row__title">Eliminate screen glare without closing a single blind</h3>
            <p class="of-row__body">If your team fights over the desk furthest from the west windows every afternoon, you've already measured the productivity cost of glare. The <a href="https://www.osha.gov/etools/computer-workstations/workstation-environment" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OSHA Computer Workstations eTool</a> identifies excessive glare as a direct cause of eye strain and headaches — a recognized workplace ergonomic hazard. Employees tilt monitors, squint through headaches, and close blinds, creating a dim, cave-like workspace.</p>
            <p class="of-row__body"><a href="/benefits/glare-reduction/">Glare-reduction window film</a> selectively filters the wavelengths responsible for screen glare while preserving full natural daylight and outdoor views. The Vista SpectraSelect VS70 reduces glare 22% while maintaining 70% visible light transmission — the light feels the same; the harsh edge that hits your monitor is gone.</p>
            <ul class="of-row__bullets">
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                Up to 83% glare reduction on high-reflectance films (LLumar R15)
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                Spectrally selective options maintain 70%+ VLT — rooms stay bright
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                Immediate results from day one — no reconfiguring desks or monitor positions
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 4: Security Film — text LEFT, image RIGHT -->
        <div class="of-row of-row--rev">
          <div class="of-row__image">
            <img
              src="/images/office-security-window-film.jpg"
              alt="Security window film holding shattered glass intact on a commercial office door — fragment retention in action"
              width="680" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="of-row__text">
            <div class="of-row__eyebrow">Benefit 04 · Security Film</div>
            <h3 class="of-row__title">Hold glass together when it matters most</h3>
            <p class="of-row__body">Standard glass shatters explosively on impact — flying fragments are among the leading causes of injury in break-ins, storms, and accidents. Security window film doesn't make glass unbreakable, but it holds shattered panes in the frame and dramatically reduces the danger of flying shards.</p>
            <p class="of-row__body">The 3M ScotchShield Ultra S800 — an 8-mil micro-layered film — is certified to ANSI Z97.1 safety glazing standards, GSA TS01-2003 blast mitigation requirements, and ASTM F1642. For ground-floor Philadelphia offices, medical facilities, and government-adjacent buildings, it's a sensible, insurance-eligible security upgrade at a fraction of laminated glass replacement cost.</p>
            <ul class="of-row__bullets">
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                3M ScotchShield Ultra S800: ANSI Z97.1 · GSA TS01 · ASTM F1642 certified
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                Slows forced entry — buys critical response time without an alarm upgrade
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                May qualify for property insurance premium reduction — ask your broker
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ FILM TYPES SLIDER ══ -->
    <section class="of-ftype" id="ofFilmTypes">
      <div class="of-ftype__track" id="ofFtypeTrack">

        <!-- SLIDE 01: Solar Control -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide of-ftype-active" data-slide="0">
          <img src="/images/office-slider-solar-control.jpg" alt="Solar control window film on Philadelphia commercial office building glass curtain wall" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">01</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Solar Control Film.
Reject Heat at the Glass.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">The workhorse of office window film. Solar control film blocks incoming solar heat before it enters your building — reducing HVAC load, eliminating hot spots, and cutting summer cooling costs by up to 30%. Available in reflective, neutral, and spectrally selective finishes across 3M, LLumar, Vista, and Solar Gard.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How dark will the tint be?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>We carry options from nearly invisible (VLT 70%+) to moderate tint (VLT 35–50%). The 3M Prestige 70 — our most popular office film — maintains 70% visible light while still rejecting 50% of solar heat. We bring samples to every site visit so you can see exactly how it looks on your glass.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will it affect the building's appearance from outside?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Spectrally selective films (like 3M Prestige series) are nearly invisible from the exterior — they add no reflective or tinted appearance. Dual-reflective and mirror-finish options are also available for buildings where a sleeker mirrored exterior look is desired.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What's the difference between VLT, SHGC, and TSER?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>VLT (Visible Light Transmission) measures how much natural light passes through. SHGC (Solar Heat Gain Coefficient) measures how much solar heat enters — lower is better. TSER (Total Solar Energy Rejected) is the inverse of SHGC expressed as a percentage. We walk you through the numbers for every film option we recommend.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Get a solar control estimate →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 02: Privacy / Frosted -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide" data-slide="1">
          <img src="/images/office-slider-privacy.jpg" alt="Frosted privacy window film on Philadelphia law firm glass-walled conference room" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">02</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Privacy Film.
Every Meeting, Confidential.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Frosted and one-way mirror films give glass-walled conference rooms, executive offices, and street-facing spaces the visual privacy they need without losing the open feel. Frosted film provides all-day, all-night privacy. One-way mirror is reflective from the outside during daylight hours while preserving outward views for those inside.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does frosted film work at night?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — frosted film provides privacy 24/7 regardless of lighting conditions. One-way mirror film relies on a brightness differential and reverses at night when interior lights are on. For conference rooms that are used after dark, frosted is the right choice.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can we still see through frosted film from inside?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Frosted film diffuses light rather than blocking it — you can still perceive movement and light levels through the glass, but clear visual detail is blocked from both sides. Think of it like etched glass. For complete opacity on all sides, blackout film is also available.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can it be applied to interior glass partitions?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — frosted and decorative films are ideal for interior partitions, glass office doors, and cubicle glass dividers. Interior glass doesn't face the same thermal stress as exterior windows, so your film options are broader. 3M FASARA offers 100+ interior-specific designs.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Explore privacy film options →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 03: Security / Safety -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide" data-slide="2">
          <img src="/images/office-slider-security.jpg" alt="Security window film on Philadelphia commercial office building ground floor entrance" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">03</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Security Film.
Glass Stays. Danger Doesn't.</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Security window film holds shattered glass in the frame on impact — dramatically reducing injury risk from flying fragments and slowing forced entry. The 3M ScotchShield Ultra S800 (8 mil) meets ANSI Z97.1, GSA TS01-2003, and ASTM F1642 standards. An essential upgrade for ground-floor Philadelphia offices, medical facilities, and government-adjacent buildings.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does security film prevent break-ins?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Security film doesn't make glass unbreakable, but it significantly slows forced entry — glass that would shatter in seconds with bare hands takes considerably longer to breach when film is installed. This delay is often enough to trigger alarm response. Film is not bulletproof and not designed to stop determined entry with tools.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does it qualify for an insurance reduction?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Some commercial property insurers offer premium reductions for documented security upgrades. Security window film installation is a physical hardening measure that your broker may recognize. We provide written documentation of the film type, certification standards met, and installation date for your records.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is 3M Impact Protection Sealant required?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>For windstorm, break-and-entry, and blast mitigation applications, 3M ScotchShield Ultra series requires 3M Impact Protection Attachment (IPA) Sealant along the window frame perimeter. We include this in our assessment and proposal for any security film application.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Get a security film estimate →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

